{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Pi3DAYG8wLAxacFoxD3bxP","type":"tool_result","content":"total 36\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 ..\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 5165 Jun  1 13:46 bhshell.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  835 Jun  1 13:46 dynamicarr.c\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 include\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 2724 Jun  1 13:46 input.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  197 Jun  1 13:46 main.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  400 Jun  1 13:46 xalloc.c\n---\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 ..\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 2998 Jun  1 13:46 test.c\n---\nCC = gcc\nCFLAGS = -Wall -Wextra -Wno-unused-variable -Wno-unused-parameter -fprofile-arcs -ftest-coverage -fPIC\nLDFLAGS = -lgcov --coverage\n\nSRC = src/bhshell.c src/dynamicarr.c src/input.c src/main.c src/xalloc.c\nTEST_SRC = src/dynamicarr.c src/input.c src/xalloc.c tests/test.c\nOBJ = $(SRC:.c=.o)\nTEST_OBJ = $(TEST_SRC:.c=.o)\n\nall: bhshell\n\nbhshell: $(SRC)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $(SRC) -o bhshell $(LDFLAGS)\n\ntest: $(TEST_SRC)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $(TEST_SRC) -o test_1 $(LDFLAGS)\n\t./test_1\n\ncoverage: test\n\t@gcov -b -c $(SRC)\n\nclean:\n\trm -rf test_1 bhshell\n\trm -rf **/*.gcno **/*.gcda **/*.gcov\n\trm -rf *.gcno *.gcda *.gcov\n\trm -rf src/*.o tests/*.o\n\n.PHONY: all clean test coverage\n---\n# A Simple Shell\nA shell written in C to help understand processes.\n\n## Features\nHas 3 built in commands => [cd, help, exit].\\\nAlso supports redirection and piping.\\\nSo, a command like `ping -c 5 google.com | grep rtt > response.txt` works.\nBut, multiple pipes are not supported.\n\n## Build\n`git clone https://github.com/bsach64/bhshell.git`\\\n`cd bhshell`\\\n`make bhshell`\\\nIf you want to run tests\\\n    `make test`\\\n`./bhshell`\n\n## TODO\n- [x] Understand how creating processes actually works\n- [x] Simulate the \"|\" operator\n- [x] Rewrite for better organisation and error handling\n    - [x] Rewrite to use xmalloc\n    - [x] Add tests\n- [x] prompt shows current working directory\n- [x] Remove `exit(EXIT_FAILURE)`\n- [x] Rewrite the Parser {Basically}\n    - [x] Simulate the \">\" operator of $BASH\n    - [x] Allow for the \"|\" operator of $BASH\n- [ ] Maybe\n    - [ ] Support multiple \">\" {allowing for `ls > file1.txt > file2.txt`}\n    - [ ] Escape characters etc {echo \"wow\" should print wow instead of \"wow\"}\n    - [ ] Implement some level of globbing (Meaning *.txt means all .txt files in the current dir)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff3bce05-d2e9-47a6-a28d-720e943409f7","uuid":"943fc5c1-0c6a-478c-beaa-b51ad298b25c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T13:46:56.627Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 36\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 ..\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 5165 Jun  1 13:46 bhshell.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  835 Jun  1 13:46 dynamicarr.c\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 include\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 2724 Jun  1 13:46 input.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  197 Jun  1 13:46 main.c\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon  400 Jun  1 13:46 xalloc.c\n---\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 scheschb amazon 4096 Jun  1 13:46 ..\n-rw------- 1 scheschb amazon 2998 Jun  1 13:46 test.c\n---\nCC = gcc\nCFLAGS = -Wall -Wextra -Wno-unused-variable -Wno-unused-parameter -fprofile-arcs -ftest-coverage -fPIC\nLDFLAGS = -lgcov --coverage\n\nSRC = src/bhshell.c src/dynamicarr.c src/input.c src/main.c src/xalloc.c\nTEST_SRC = src/dynamicarr.c src/input.c src/xalloc.c tests/test.c\nOBJ = $(SRC:.c=.o)\nTEST_OBJ = $(TEST_SRC:.c=.o)\n\nall: bhshell\n\nbhshell: $(SRC)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $(SRC) -o bhshell $(LDFLAGS)\n\ntest: $(TEST_SRC)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $(TEST_SRC) -o test_1 $(LDFLAGS)\n\t./test_1\n\ncoverage: te